<p>The United States and Japan unveiled the first slate of projects—worth about $36 billion—under a broader $550 billion trade and investment framework that President Trump says will steer Japanese financing into US industry and energy infrastructure. The initial list includes natural gas-related facilities and a synthetic industrial diamond facility. Some reports also pointed to either a critical minerals site or an oil export facility among the first projects, with locations mentioned including Ohio, Georgia and Texas and the Gulf of Mexico. Washington and Tokyo are pitching the plan as both a commercial bet and an economic-security play, with a focus on energy supplies and critical minerals. Trump tied the investment push to his tariff strategy in a social media post, while Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi described the projects as strengthening the allies’ economic security partnership. The debut projects suggest momentum, but some coverage noted that early announcements left key details—such as the exact financing structures—unclear.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/u6U_Leq1SMB5Nj5lNxx4AfGXIAZ9NPQ6OAyTUFdeJvIZLknUu3KCEY5O66ZjFW2faY48v8tc5ZyP-lkqJVCixOfL4-mZnpSFB5veyslQqlqu8aMh2gvUKz-wfsP6nJobleKAeGGS9Kep-4v3jFsu1BobDfBYA0phmVDUlfA2i5NB3WcmQJkXGbcLppfddrSCvHbEreO0ahvuU-uKAHygJbbKe9GB3Mcdlt_b17KMKfic7LFDgZY-SOUVcFmKnuDMGmBZLuoeu9k-4Q' alt='US President Donald Trump (left) and Japan’s Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi in Tokyo on Oct. 28, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Different reported ‘trios’: Coverage and official communications did not all name the same three projects—SCMP cited an Ohio gas power plant plus a Georgia critical-minerals site and a Texas LNG facility, while The Hindu cited an Ohio gas facility, a Gulf of Mexico crude oil export facility and a synthetic industrial diamond manufacturing facility; FT highlighted oil, natural gas and synthetic diamond facilities.</li><li>Ohio power plant: One featured project is a natural gas-fired power plant in Portsmouth, Ohio that the Trump administration billed as the largest natural gas-fired generating facility in US history.</li><li>Gulf exports: US government communications also cited a crude oil export facility in the Gulf of Mexico as part of the opening tranche.</li><li>Timing: SCMP said the projects were unveiled in the weeks before Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi was set to meet President Trump.</li><li>Trump’s framing: The Guardian reported that Trump said the deals would “end our foolish dependence on foreign sources,” framing the initiative in economic-security terms.</li></ul><blockquote>Japan is now officially, and financially, moving forward with the first set of investments under its $550 billion commitment to invest in the United States of America - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He framed the debut projects as Japan moving forward with its investment commitment and explicitly credited “TARIFFS” as enabling the move. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/18/trump-announces-japan-s-first-36-billion-investment-in-the-us_6750600_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi: She hailed the US-Japan announcements as enhancing “economic security,” according to coverage of the joint unveiling. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/feb/18/us-japan-critical-minerals-agreement-oil-gas-projects-deal'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Financial Times framing: FT described the initial set of oil, natural gas and synthetic diamond facilities as a marker of “crucial progress” from broad pledges to concrete projects. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/96bc9b3d-150d-4a21-8be9-29bdf45695af'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>SCMP reporting: SCMP emphasized that the announcement offered limited detail on the financing mechanics and noted the projects were unveiled ahead of a planned Trump–Takaichi meeting. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3343852/trump-unveils-first-japan-investments-under-trade-deal-us'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/18/trump-announces-japan-s-first-36-billion-investment-in-the-us_6750600_4.html'>Trump announces Japan&#x27;s $36 billion investment in the US</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/96bc9b3d-150d-4a21-8be9-29bdf45695af'>US and Japan unveil first mega-projects under $550bn trade deal</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3343852/trump-unveils-first-japan-investments-under-trade-deal-us'>Trump unveils first Japan investments under trade deal with US</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/feb/18/us-japan-critical-minerals-agreement-oil-gas-projects-deal'>US and Japan unveil $36bn of oil, gas and critical minerals projects in challenge to China</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/trump-announces-first-tranche-of-japans-investments-in-us-industry-under-550bn-trade-pact-13980925.html'>Trump announces first tranche of Japan&#x27;s investments in US industry under $550bn trade pact</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-unveils-first-japan-investments-under-trade-pact/article70645098.ece'>Trump unveils first Japan investments under trade pact</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>